cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you reference or build on CROA, please cite the specification via its Zenodo DOI.
  The DOI below is the v1.0.1 deposit, published 4 September 2026 and carrying the corpus
  as it stood on 3 September. The repository has moved since: see CHANGELOG.md [1.0.1] and
  spec/errata-v1.0.md for the differences between the deposited document and this working
  baseline. Cite the DOI for the record; read the repository for the current text.
title: "CROA — Constrained Reachability Orchestration Architecture: A Framework for Deterministic Governance of Agentic AI Execution"
abstract: >-
  CROA is a vendor-neutral architecture framework for the governed execution of agentic AI systems.
  Within the modeled action space, under the registered invariant set, and given network-enforced
  execution-boundary containment, an agent cannot, by its own choice, reach a state that violates a
  registered invariant — such execution paths are structurally unreachable, the sole exception being a
  governed, signed authorization. Published for the community to test, challenge, and improve; the
  reference harness demonstrates the mechanism and is not evidence that a deployment has these
  properties.
